.TH "OSTRYA\-RECEIVE" "1" "" "ostrya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ostrya\-receive \- Receive one push session over standard input and standard output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ostrya receive [OPTIONS]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Receive one push session over standard input and standard output.
.PP
By default, \fB\%ostrya push\fR runs this command on the server over ssh. At start, the command reads and checks the client groups, the server group, the trust groups, and the key groups of the repository config, and a bad group ends it with status \%1. The session selects no client group, so it opens no push session: \fB\%Hello\fR gets \fB\%ref\-denied\fR\&. Standard output carries the frames of the session alone. For each warning of the session, the command writes one \fB\%warning: STEP: MESSAGE\fR line to standard error. It writes nothing else, also under \%\-\-verbose. The exit status is \%0 after a committed session, also with warnings, and \%1 otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
The global options are listed in \fBostrya\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBostrya\fR(1)
